       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and the risk is lactic acidosis. Kidney and liver function are normal, but that doesn't make this dose safe.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day in total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose**, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg per administration.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intended, please confirm that. I'd also suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
